  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOCARIBE-GOOS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOCARIBE&#x2019;s GOOS Programme helps countries in the Caribbean and Tropical Americas strengthen ocean observation, forecasting, and early warning systems to better respond to hurricanes, coastal flooding, climate change, and other marine hazards, and to support sustainable development of the Blue Economy. The programme promotes regional cooperation, shared monitoring systems, and improved access to ocean information for decision-making and public safety. Key activities include expanding observation networks, developing pilot sites, supporting coastal resilience projects, training experts, engaging fishing communities in data collection, and improving cooperation between regional and global partners. Expected deliverables include stronger forecasting capacity, regional observation plans, technical training, new partnerships, shared ocean data, and improved early warning and coastal management systems.</narrative>
  </description>
